post.append('## Selected installation and unchanged acceptance')
post.append(f"{ID} has **one complete UR5e, one carriage and one wall lane**. The entire helper, its carriage and its chain were removed from the compiled model; no invisible parked helper is assumed. The full principal mounts at Y={c['front_mount_y']:.3f}, Z={c['height']:.3f} m, tilted {c['mount_deg']}°. The rail is at Z={c['rail_centres_z'][0]:.3f} m; the complete chain cover is centered at Y={c['chain_y']:.4f}, Z={c['chain_centres_z'][0]:.4f} m. Only the first lane/chain entry is active when count=1. The full power track moves to Z={c['power_z']:.3f} m. No portal, front legs, elevator, pallet, taller wall or wider wall is present. The original 3.7 m wall, 0.85 m counter, sink, stove exclusion and upper cabinets remain.")
post.append('Acceptance remains 5 mm / 3°, PAD=0, 10 mm robot/environment and inter-arm gaps, ordinary 5 mm held/gripper/environment gaps, μ=0.5, SF=1.5, 150 N key force and 15 Nm key moment. **Every robot part, including fingers, uses 10 mm against full door sweeps.** Only named wall-bracket rear mating faces can touch the wall. Doors themselves are not tested against the person corridor. The copied R05 checker/planner/source assets remain unchanged; R07 adapters and their own derivatives contain the changes. [Binding decisions](../../DECISIONS.md), [active contact ledger](../../sim/r07/integrator/results/intended_contacts.json).')
post.append('The fixed **GROHE Eurocube 13303000** wall spout replaces the tall deck mixer. Its public drawing gives 170 mm outlet projection, 60 mm square escutcheon and 8 mm mounting depth. The conservative complete 60 × 200 × 60 mm external cover includes the nose beyond the outlet axis; concealed connector, plumbing and the normally closed valve enclosure remain modeled. It is a full dimensional reservation, not OEM casting CAD. The wall connection is '+str(c['replacement_faucet']['wall_connection_m'])+' m. The falling-jet reference is a design point below the conservative cover, not a measured outlet offset. [Manufacturer-authored drawing](https://www.larochenigeria.com/shop/img/product-docs/Product35617_20220616.pdf), [buyable listing](https://www.oeg.net/en/grohe-universal-cube-bath-spout-for-wall-mounting-800020267). The retained [DFRobot FIT0498 valve](https://www.dfrobot.com/product-1530.html) needs potable-material, dry-enclosure, flow and shutoff qualification; electric commands do not need knob motions.')
post.append('## Arm and appliance choices')
post.append('| Candidate | Public capability | Decision |\n|---|---|---|\n| UR5e | 5 kg, 850 mm reach | Selected; full meshes/inertia, actual mounted rated-payload envelope, principal 3 kg plus 1.2 kg EOAT retained. |\n| xArm6 | 5 kg nominal, 700 mm reach | Full model compared in L41 and earlier paired maps. Its long-offset payload limit with this EOAT does not qualify 3 kg + EOAT as principal. Optional capped helper adds clutter and was removed. |\n| UR3e | 3 kg, 500 mm reach | Smaller helper candidate; cannot meet principal 3 kg plus positive EOAT. No invented reduced UR5e geometry. |')
post.append('The [xArm manual](https://www.ufactory.cc/wp-content/uploads/2023/05/xArm-User-Manual-V2.0.0.pdf) and [UR3e specifications](https://www.universal-robots.com/products/ur3e/) support the comparisons. UR5e mounted payload-envelope and documented power-loss holding evidence are inherited; no continuous-torque publication requirement is reinstated. Rail braking remains de-energize-to-apply. Compiled mass is retained rather than rescaled to brochure nominal mass. Alternate JAKA/Elite/Dobot/AUBO candidates remain in the prior public-source screen; no new matched-model numerical pass is claimed for them.')
post.append('The commodity screen considered **Sammic M-5**, **Starfrit Rotato Express**, **Nemco 55550-8**, retained **Breville BFP610**, R211 XL and HENDI 229200. [Research and dimension record](../../sim/r07/integrator/results/research_v4.json).')
post.append('The [Sammic M-5](https://sammic.com/en/product/m-5) is 333 × 367 × 490 mm, 300 W, 15.5 kg, with 5 kg capacity and a 0–6 minute timer; the OEM explicitly includes carrots and potatoes. Its complete conservative box interferes with the left chain band, and the far-right bay has poorer reach. This rejects those layouts, not every possible exact M-5 casting placement. Its loading lid, interior and small-batch peeling depth/loss were not qualified.')
post.append('The selected **Rotato Express 093209** concept occupies a complete **300 × 300 × 350 mm guarded design reservation** on the left counter. The [OEM product](https://www.starfrit.com/en/starfrit-electric-rotato-express) and [manual](https://www.starfrit.com/media/pdf/instrbooklet--User-manual-093209002BLCK-en2.pdf) describe the mechanism; the [supplier dimensions](https://www.odpbusiness.com/a/products/983762/Starfrit-Rotato-Express/) list 6 × 6 × 10.5 inches with ambiguous axis ordering. The reservation exceeds every listed dimension in any order. It is not matched OEM mechanism CAD and no access hole was invented. The OEM requires food longer than 140 mm to be halved: the 160 mm carrot therefore adds a guarded pre-cut and conserved-piece obligation. Lowering/raising the holder, setting cutter height, rocking food off the spike and removing eyes remain explicit events. Carrot suitability, peeling depth, gouging and yield remain unqualified. Four passing approach templates cannot establish those operations.')
post.append('The full **BFP610** 395 × 295 × 395 mm reservation remains on the counter, shifted back 55 mm to improve the front-edge reserve. [OEM page](https://www.breville.com/en-nz/product/bfp610), [manual](https://assets.breville.com/BFP610/BFP610_ANZ_WEB_IB_A23_LR.pdf). It is a batch machine: motor stop, unplugging, lid removal, disc removal and bowl unloading are retained. It receives no R211 continuous-discharge credit. Exact interlock/pusher/chute geometry and feed force remain unqualified. The [Nemco eight-wedger](https://nemco.com/catalog/easy-wedger/) is 203.2 × 203.2 × 482.6 mm; exposed sharp manual operation would need a sourced actuator/guard interface. It was screened, not installed. The existing guarded secondary cutter remains for greens and tomato; its sourced loads were not lowered.')
post.append('The retained below-counter solid named `m5_water_drain_service` is an unused conservative service reservation from the appliance screen, not an OEM Rotato drain assembly. Appliance covers reserve the full public dimensions, but the new peeler and processor interfaces lack matched mechanism geometry. This is an explicit qualification blocker, not permission to load through a solid cover.')
